# Normalise line endings so a Windows checkout matches CI.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf` leaves CRLF in the working tree while the repo
# stores LF. Git hides the difference, but tools that read files directly do
# not: `mix credo --strict` fails locally on "windows line endings" while the
# same commit passes on Linux CI. Forcing eol=lf keeps the local gate honest.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
